#~ msgid "How the numbers were made: one simulation — 24 players, 4 courts, 100 rounds — replayed across 7 seeds in three synthetic rooms: varied (skills spread across the range, plus a ringer and a beginner), typical (about a 1.0 DUPR spread), and tight (a bunched pack). True skills are not frozen: as in a real club, about 20% of players improve slightly over the session, one improves fast enough to cross most of the pack, and one slowly gets worse — the same players in every strategy's run, so the comparison stays fair. Every round is a real solve through the same optimiser the app uses. Charts are 5-round rolling averages across all seeds; headline numbers summarise the last 25 rounds. Charts are interactive — hover for values, click a strategy to isolate its line."
