#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:904
#, fuzzy
#~ msgid "Ratings do not settle until 30–40 rounds in, and a single session lasts 10–12: by the time ratings become useful, the session has ended. I want to explore using score differentials to accelerate cold starts — potentially producing usable ratings within a round or two of an unrated player's first game. The risk is that this is itself a form of oracle: reading more into a result than it actually says could tamper with convergence rather than speed it up."
#~ msgstr "評分會持續精準化 30–40 輪——即兩到三場活動——雖然配對品質在第 5 輪就已優於基準，但真正從零開始的頭十幾輪仍是球會生命中最顛簸的階段。我想探索用比分差距來縮短這段期間——有機會在無評分球員打完一兩場後就產生可用的評分。目前循環賽工具已支援手動指定球員排名。風險在於這本身也是一種先知模式：從結果中解讀出超過其真實含意的資訊，可能會干擾收斂，而非加速它。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:851
#, fuzzy
#~ msgid "The Oracle knows everyone's real skill and hand-balances every match. It is in the field to demonstrate one thing: rigging matches by what you know prevents the ratings from ever learning it. Strong players are always split and cancel each other out, so no informative result ever arrives — the Oracle posts the best match quality of any strategy and the worst ladder accuracy, stuck seven to eight places off forever."
#~ msgstr "先知模式知道每個人的真實實力，並親手平衡每一場對戰。它出現在測試中只為證明一件事：依你已知的資訊操控對戰，會讓評分永遠學不到東西。強者總是被拆開並互相抵銷，因此永遠不會出現有資訊價值的結果——先知模式的對戰品質是所有策略中最好的，排名準確度卻是最差的，永遠卡在約七個名次的誤差。美式開放打法中「餓死」的排名，正是同樣的效應在無意間、以較輕微的劑量發生。"

